{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","title":"Persistence","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"externalID":"Persistence"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record on disk until it is delivered, so the records a tracker tracked survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"],"anchor":"Stores"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, a tracker keeps its records in memory only. A tracker given a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker(store:)"},{"type":"text","text":") appends each record to it as the tracker’s worker reaches the record, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishing it, and starts its records with the ones the store kept from earlier runs."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the store this module ships: a directory of append-only segment files, bounded at 5 MiB unless you pass another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":". A segment is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted once every record in it is delivered."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore()"},{"text":" keeps every event type declared with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" in the program’s modules, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library’s own; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore(events:)"},{"text":" keeps only the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" types it lists. Each record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a CBOR (RFC 8949) map, its event a map of its properties under their names, written through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformance. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"text":", part of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":") writes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the conformance, and Swift’s synthesized one works too. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" writes a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"text":" property, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"date in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date]"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Date?]"},{"text":", as the seconds since 2001 it stores, so it reads back exactly. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"text":" written through the CBOR package’s own form, in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" type of your own or in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"synthesized conformance, reads back to within a rounding of a microsecond’s scale. Events of other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types, such as one that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" by hand without being listed, are delivered in this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run but never written, and reported once as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store doesn’t read the records Traffluent 0.0.44 or earlier wrote, in an earlier format:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" deletes their segments and reports each as a corruption."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each drop is reported on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the oldest segments"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deleted to stay under the bound, a write that failed, and records recovery couldn’t read or found"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at another "},{"code":"schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A record whose delivery had started when the app ended comes back with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set. Call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", after the tracker’s "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app moves to the background, so the records written so far survive power loss too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An app on Apple platforms that already keeps a GRDB database can keep its records in a table of it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"DatabaseStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRDBPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\")","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int = 1","}","","let store = try SegmentStore(directory: directory, byteBound: 1024 * 1024)","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\", seats: 3))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/persistingrecords","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what the store writes, its bounds and recovery, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers which changes to an event’s type its stored records can be read through.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"title":"SegmentStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","title":"DropReport","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","title":"RecordStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A store keeping events of the types ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directory"},{"text":"; it recovers the records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already there.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"events"},{"kind":"text","te